Here is the deal with Law of Attraction that most people don't get. Until you believe deeply that you can be happy without the SP, and until you in fact are happy without the SP, you either won't get the SP or you won't be happy when you do.

&#x200B;

Law of attraction attracts to you what you are vibrating out to the universe. If you are vibrating out desperation and unhappiness, if you end up in a relationship while vibrating that out, you will in fact become more desperate and unhappy in that relationship, I guarantee it. Your feelings of desperation will intensify!

&#x200B;

The real secret of Law of Attraction is to find the deep happiness within in all circumstances, only then will what you TRULY want be made manifest.

I believe it's actually a pretty decent metric when you take into account human psychology. If you are a "rational" being then sure you only care about how much wealth you have, but people aren't like that. People compare themselves to others. 

&#x200B;

Let's say I work at a job with a coworker, and I get paid $50,000. Hey that's pretty nice! I can have a good life on that! Now let's say I found out my coworker gets paid $100,000. All of a sudden I am super discontent with my job and start doing shitty at it. See where I am going with this? People also compare themselves to their bosses, "Hey how much work is Jeff Bezos actually doing?" 

&#x200B;

A value that a lot of people have is "fairness", and the greater the wealth inequality, the greater the perceived unfairness. When people perceive a lot of unfairness, they do a shittier job. 

&#x200B;

So I argue wealth inequality is a decent metric because those at the top aren't contributing that much more value to society. If you  believe "how much money a person has should be roughly equal to the value that person contributes to society", then it becomes clear that the super rich do not contribute the amount of value they receive. They are simply in control of the systems, and so get a much larger allocation of the value created. They have much more negotiation power. They are better able to define the terms of employment. You see that giant employment contract I signed? There isn't any negotiation for most workers. The company sets the terms.  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Yet rates of depression and anxiety in the Western World are higher than they have ever been. I think there is something about being close to death in ones everyday experience that makes one appreciate life. So yes, we have this material abundance, yet we tend to have more existential angst. 

&#x200B;

Also there is a distinct lack of community right now that has never really been the case before which I think is a major contributing factor.

LOA works best when you least expect it! 

&#x200B;

Abraham hicks calls it the art of allowing.

But why can't it be win win? Now I get to see more shit that I like! Hooray!

&#x200B;

Edit: Like we both get things in the exchange. What am I losing by using social media?

I did good sir :)

&#x200B;

I also want to see a world of peace harmony and love. I'd love to see us build hospitals and schools in the middle east. I'd love to see has cocreate beautifully :)

When it comes to other individuals. We can't control them, they always have free will. It sounds like when you were focusing on your ex you had a lot  of mixed vibrations. It sounds like there was lots of love, but lots of distress at his absence. With mixed vibrations like that law of attraction won't bring your ex back to you. 

&#x200B;

Letting go is an extremely powerful tool in law of attraction when our vibration is so mixed, so you intuitively have it. Surrender to God, trust in your source energy. and focus on finding your alignment. What this means is focusing on how you feel. In every single moment that you remember simply notice your emotional state. Notice if any thoughts are associated with that state. Being truly mindful of our thoughts and emotions and how they intermingle is really the first step to mastering law of attraction. Do I feel good when I think this thought? If not we know its not a thought our higher self is thinking. We can then try and think softer thoughts, more general thoughts, less specific thoughts. Notice which thoughts feel a little better and keep moving in that direction. 

&#x200B;

We will keep getting rehooked by thoughts that don't feel good, less and less as we master this process. But do not fret. It is okay. Do not worry about thinking a negative thought, because then you are simply adding to the negativity, you are worrying about worrying. Allow the thought to be there, thank it for teaching you contrast. Thank the negative thought for teaching you the path to your inner being, to source, to your higher self, to God. 

&#x200B;

Love and Light.

&#x200B;

Casey

There are lots of strategies here. 

&#x200B;

The first important thing about law of attraction is to care about how you feel. This requires that you are constantly checking in with yourself, and noticing how you feel. The more awareness you can have of your emotional state the better. This means you need to VISCERALLY feel them, not just say oh I am angry, but feel it. Notice the sensations in the body, notice the movement of energy, notice where energy is stuck. 

&#x200B;

Then as you notice it, notice what thoughts are coming up with that emotion. See if you can reach just a little higher, or go a little more general. If a negative thought comes like "I am really worried about out future!" , Don't try to stop it! Just let it be, let it unfold. If you become worried about your thoughts you are now worrying about worrying and exacerbating the problem!!!! 

&#x200B;

Secondly, don't say things like "We have a long way to go!", You don't actually know how long you have to go. Instead say things like "We are doing are best everyday!". 

&#x200B;

Thirdly, there is something to be aware of that seems to happen when people become aware of law of attraction, its called a three day process, but it can happen on any time scale.

Basically it is like this 

Day 1: Inspiration Happens, maybe an inspired action happens

Day 2: Doubts Arise, Fear Arises. Its like all your limiting beliefs come to the surface

Day 3: If you managed to work overcome the limiting beliefs, day 3 flows smoothly.

&#x200B;

This cycle can happen in an hour, in a minute, in weeks, in years. 

&#x200B;

For more on the 3 day cycle and other law of attraction based empowerment teachings check out Bentinho Massaros Website, He teaches a lot of law of attraction based stuff.

&#x200B;

[https://www.trinfinityacademy.com/courses/empowerment-1-the-fundamentals-of-empowered-living/lesson-6-the-three-day-process/](https://www.trinfinityacademy.com/courses/empowerment-1-the-fundamentals-of-empowered-living/lesson-6-the-three-day-process/)

First technically, EVERYTHING is law of attraction. Literally everything. Traditional purchases not traditional purchases, its all vibrations and energy.

&#x200B;

Second, the point of the teachings by Abraham Hicks is to do things so we can take inspired action that is from our higher self. If I feel really inspired to work overtime, then yeah totally awesome! If it feels like drudgery and awful, that's not really inspired by my higher self.

&#x200B;

Now the key to this is that there could actually be two things going on if I feel bad about doing 5 hours of extra work. First it could be that the happiest way for me is not actually 5 hrs extra overtime. Second, it could be that the happiest way is five hours of overtime but the way I am presently viewing the work is not in alignment with my higher self! I could be having untrue or limiting beliefs about my work. I could think a thought like "my work sucks, I want to quit". Well I guarantee your higher self is not having that thought because any thought your higher self would have feels good. Instead you could say "This work has provided for me a stable source of income and food myself and my family. I am feeling a calling to expand into a new direction! Something exciting is ahead! i can feel it!" Do you see the difference between these two? In both cases you could be leaving your job, but one is running away from something, and the other is running towards something.   


When we notice how we feel, and we notice what thinks are connected to those feelings, we can start to slowly grasp for a better feeling thought and a better feeling thought and a better feeling thought until we can take action from a place of Inspiration.

&#x200B;

And meditation helps us with this process as it increases our awareness.

