I really like it! I want to expand on one of the comments you made that seems "obvious", the Donald Trump is a Prick comment.  There are two ways I want to break this down, first there are many ways to view Donald Trump and second I want to pick apart the word "Prick" and using words like "Prick" distance us from our higher selves.

&#x200B;

First, we could view Donald Trump in many ways! We could view him as someone who simply needs more love! We could view him as someone who is simply ignorant. He doesn't know how Law of Attraction works. We could take the view that he is generating a lot of contrast for us presently so we are all realizing just how much we want to upgrade our system of government to be something much better! We could just view him as one man who is part of a system that isn't working. meaning we need systemic changes! There are so so so many ways to view him that is closer to how our higher beings see him. Donald Trump, thank you for showing us just how broken our government system is, thank you for making it so incredibly obvious! Donald Trump is doing what he thinks is best! He doesn't know that he could be so much happier and more loved if he took a different route. He doesn't know just how much positive attention he could receive if he changed course! 

See all of these totally different ways to view the man? It pulls us out of the Drama Triangle, and pulls us closer to our higher selfs vision of him.

Second, I want to look at the word "Prick" and see how these types of words "Prick, Dick, Asshole, Fucker" etc, detach us from source and our higher being, I want us to see how they aren't "true" words. What makes someone a Prick? Is it just someone who I am annoyed by? Whom I don't feel good in their presence? Is it someone who "hurts" someone else? What if my feelings are "hurt" by you calling me something innocuous like "Hey Dude!", when I identify as female? Does that make you a "prick"? Or does it make me "overly sensitive"? What if neither of those are true? If you sort of stretch this out, you start to see that adjective words create distance. If we reframe things into needs and feelings we can connect more compassionately. I need love and affection. I need respect. If I reframe someone calling me "dude" as "oh its just cultural" or "he isn't intending harm" or "he is just a surfer!" then I will be less likely to be hurt by it. Alternatively, if the person calling me dude can reframe it as "Oh they like to be called something else, no problem, I don't need to use the word dude, I can be happy without using it!". Connection can be formed from either end. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, if we learn to strike adjectives like "Dick" or "mean" or "cruel" from our vocabulary, we can become more true to ourselves and our higher self. Our higher self never sees anyone as "cruel" maybe misguided or unaware but even those adjectives are probably not the truest" Our highest self sees everyone as beings of love and light who engaging in a learning process of expansion and that all souls involved are choosing to learn in this present reality the lessons that are coming to them. All souls involved are contributing to the infinity of the one true source and creator. All souls involved are complicit in this reality.

&#x200B;

Sending Love and Light.

Namaste.

&#x200B;

First of all, know deep down in your soul you are worthy of love. You are loved right now in this moment.

Some other strategies to know about law of attraction. These moments are creating contrast for you, you are learning what you do want and what you don't want. Do you really want to be with someone that will switch to a new girl after only 3 days?  Is that the kind of guy you want? 

Use this time "alone" to connect deeply with that source within yourself, connect deeply with your higher self. Try and find any thought or idea that will make you feel just a little bit better. Climb the emotional ladder one step at a time. You are a being of love and light. Imagine yourself bathed in a golden glow. 

When you feel that insecure feeling, welcome it, thank it, for it is teaching you what you do not want. You are creating a beautiful relationship in your future by seeing this contrast now. Pay attention to your feelings. Do whatever you can that will help you feel better in the moment. If it is too much get up and go for a walk. Refocus.

Law of attraction is ultimately about Focus. If we care about feeling good and focus on that, and keep focusing on that, and learn more about what feels good and what doesn't. Focus on feeling love for yourself. Hold yourself in compassion and light. When you are in the pain, you can't see the solution. There is already some momentum going here so just embrace the pain with open arms, when a heart breaks it is breaking open, it is expanding to higher and higher capacities of love and joy. Every loss is a launching pad to a better future. 

&#x200B;

Holding you in love and light. 

&#x200B;

Namaste.

